 ## 2026-07-28
 
+### 1308 — Atomic install review rejected the unjournaled default adapter path
+- REVIEW: `TASK-260720-2284br` changes requested. The copy-mode transaction path passes focused rollback, concurrency, recovery, build, vet, and formatting gates, but production defaults to `adapter_mode: auto`, which selects symlink mirrors on capable filesystems.
+- FINDING: `Mirror.Link` deletes/recreates live adapter entries after `Journal.Prepare` and before `Journal.Commit`; those entries are absent from the journal. A link failure returns with a prepared journal, and recovery treats `PhasePrepared` as commit-worthy, so a later run can apply an operation that already returned `failed`. A later target rollback also cannot restore the replaced mirror.
+- FINDING: stale adapter symlinks are pruned after the transaction (and therefore after the project consumer ledger), violating consumer-last ordering and the requirement to include stale managed removals in the atomic target set.
+- TEST GAP: all shared install fixtures force `AdapterMode: "copy"`. The “every target class” sweep is one project add-only scenario and never creates forwarding-shim, mirror-ledger, removal, hybrid, or default symlink targets.
+- REQUIRED: journal symlink replacements/removals with exact reverse restoration; durably roll back every ordinary post-prepare failure; add project/global/hybrid failure sweeps covering every class plus default-auto/explicit-symlink and stale-removal cases.
+- EVIDENCE: `TASK-260720-2284br_review-verdict-cycle-1.md`. No product code modified.
+
 ### 1253 — Atomic cross-scope commit landed; adapter symlinks are the one non-journaled class
 - MILESTONE: `TASK-260720-2284br` — install phases 20–23 (consumer-first, piecemeal materialization, cleanup, adapters, GC) replaced by one manager-home-locked transaction over staged targets, consumer ledger last. New `internal/staging`, `internal/install/{commit,targets}.go`; staging producers in `envfiles`, `adapters`, `globalbins`, `scopes`, `runtimestore`.
 - FINDING: the four direct blockers had each landed in a **separate uncommitted worktree**, never in one tree. Union of `.temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0/worktree` (godriver + 3itlly staging) and `.temp/TASK-260720-31nl14/worktree` (transaction + managerlock + marker v2). 128 shared files, 10 divergent — every divergence was one chain at base while the other advanced, so the union is a per-file superset with no content merge. Built twice into independent worktrees and compared by SHA-256 manifest to prove the composition.

